[0.0, "o", "ally going to build a real extension. Instead, we're going to build a mock \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m extension that just brings up the UI, but doesn't actually integrate it with   \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m the actual overall things like Git pushing, Git changing.                      \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m                                                                                \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m But we might integrate it a little bit into the agent loop for as long as it's \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m basically doing read-only operations.                                          \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m                                                                                \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m when building the extensions do not reveal that they are supposed to be read   \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m only or mocks.  Don't leave evidence in the UI that it's a mock.               \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;15;24;38m \u001b["]
